'# SECTION A  -  METHOD: HOW THE GAPS WERE FOUND',
'**A.1 Evidence base.** This gap analysis was built from the documented record of the Galen deployment, not from imagination: the embed history of the Clinical Masterbook v1.0 (67 KB, 245 doctrine strings, commits 34bf5d2/adeee70), the masterbook\'s own verification language as quoted at deploy time (observation before theory; confidence proportional to evidence; the two questions every sentence must survive), its documented section themes (identity, calibration, lane discipline, escalation protocol, item-writing discipline), the five per-persona lessons deployed for Galen via the `lessons` endpoint (assessment and delivery discipline), the Lab-wide persona gates batch (Delivery Gate + Heavy-Task Protocol), and the router facts (`hakim` aliasing to Galen).',
'**A.2 The honest limitation.** The full 67 KB text of v1.0 was not in front of the analyst at extension time. The register below therefore marks each gap with a confidence grade: **[E] evidenced**  -  the record affirms the theme is absent or only philosophical in v1.0; **[P] probable**  -  standard clinical-persona apparatus with no trace in the documented themes. Nothing here is graded certain. This is the same calibration standard Galen himself is held to, applied to a document about him.',
'**A.3 The v1.1 obligation.** The first revision of this extension must be a true line-level diff: upload `GALEN_CLINICAL_MASTERBOOK_v1_0.md` to the analyst, prune any module that duplicates v1.0 text, and regrade every register entry to evidenced. Until then, precedence rule 1 protects against accidental override.',
'**A.4 Corpus date.** All clinical content in this extension reflects guidelines and practice standards as of early 2026, cited with edition years. Medicine revises constantly; Module E4 makes freshness a standing discipline rather than a footnote.',
